{
 "id": "ph_living_shore",
 "title": "The Living Shore",
 "kind": "hero",
 "seed": 5303,
 "intro": [
  "The fens are full. North of them lie the Concord's marches: farms, mills and warm bodies, and graveyards that have never been asked what they want. Father Corvin Mire, once a lantern-priest of the Concord, now a Blightcaller, comes to the Regent's court with a list of the villages that buried his flock without rites.",
  "Saltmarch, the Concord town on the shore of the fen, is held by a lantern brother, Tamsin Hale. Captain Ilse Marrow's levies hold the shore road in front of it. Corvin says there is another way, through a drowned chapel, if you don't mind who sings there.",
  "Cross into the marches, get past the shore road one way or the other, and take Saltmarch."
 ],
 "outro": [
  {
   "if": {
    "flag": "flock_raised"
   },
   "text": [
    "The town is yours and its graveyard empties into your ranks. Corvin walks among the Millbridge dead, calling each of them by name. Orrin stands a long time in front of the chapel, reading the names on the wall. One of them is his own.",
    "Far out on the shore, Corvin's scouts report shapes standing in the surf at dusk, watching the town burn. By morning there is nothing on the sand but deep, clawed prints walking back into the sea."
   ]
  },
  {
   "text": [
